Soundbite builds on Audiogram (github.com/drkxbt/audiogram, MIT) for the editor and the video, and on
transformers.js (Hugging Face, Apache-2.0) with ONNX Runtime Web (Microsoft, MIT) for speech recognition. The speech
model, Whisper by OpenAI (MIT), converted to ONNX by the onnx-community, is downloaded from Hugging Face when it is
first needed and is not part of this repository.

The demo page ships the Geist and Geist Mono typefaces by Vercel, in collaboration with basement.studio, in
demo/fonts/, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (demo/fonts/OFL.txt). The sample in demo/sample is Audiogram's
made-up exchange read by the Microsoft David and Microsoft Zira text-to-speech voices; it is not a recording of any
real Space or person.

The editor's fonts come from Fontsource under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, each one's licence copied next to it in
dist/app/fonts/. The photos in photos/ are in the public domain (CC0), found through Openverse and Wikimedia Commons;
photos/CREDITS.md credits each one's photographer.

Stock photos, illustrations, videos, stickers and GIFs, when the hosting page offers a search for them, come from
Pixabay, Pexels and GIPHY under each library's own licence; the panel credits the library and the author of each one.
None of them is bundled with this repository.

The animated emoji stickers in the media panel are Google's Noto Emoji animations
(googlefonts.github.io/noto-emoji-animation) under CC BY 4.0, and the panel credits Noto under the results. Each one is
fetched through the hosting page when it is picked and is not part of this repository.

The KLIPY stickers and GIFs in the media panel, when the hosting page hands Soundbite a KLIPY app key, are searched
from the visitor's browser and fetched from KLIPY (klipy.com) when they are picked, under KLIPY's terms, and the panel
credits KLIPY under the results. None of them is part of this repository.

The drawings in the Elements panel are written to dist/app/drawings/ at build time, with a licence file covering all
five sets. The brand logos come from Simple Icons (simpleicons.org) under CC0 1.0; each mark belongs to its owner and
is offered only so a clip can say where to find the show, and none of those companies has any connection with this
project. The icons are Phosphor Icons (phosphoricons.com, MIT) and the emoji are Microsoft's Fluent Emoji in the flat
style (github.com/microsoft/fluentui-emoji, MIT). The people and faces are Open Peeps and the doodles Open Doodles,
both by Pablo Stanley (openpeeps.com, opendoodles.com) under CC0 1.0, as packaged in @dicebear/open-peeps and
react-open-doodles.

The 3D icons in the Elements panel are 3dicons by Vijay Verma (3dicons.co, github.com/realvjy/3dicons), dedicated to
the public domain under CC0 1.0. The build fetches the renders from the project's own CDN and writes them, as WebP, to
dist/app/objects3d/ with a licence note; the panel credits 3dicons under the results.

X is named only to say what the clips are for; X Corp. has no connection with this project. Google Ad Manager serves
the optional rewarded ad on drk.vc's copy; Google has no connection with this project either.
